        "original_id": "8179e1aa-2771-53cc-b713-b378725047f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. P. Lovecraft, Timothy Leary, August Derleth, Donald Wandrei\n- Organizations: Arkham House\n- Places: Sauk City, Wisconsin\n- Products: Slan\n- Topics: horror fiction, psychedelic drugs, weird fiction\n\nFacts:\n- H. P. Lovecraft was born on August 20, 1890, and was an American author who achieved posthumous fame through influential horror fiction.\n- Arkham House was founded in 1939 in Sauk City, Wisconsin, by August Derleth and Donald Wandrei to preserve the best fiction of H. P. Lovecraft in hardcover.\n- Slan was published in hardcover by Arkham House in 1946 in an edition of 4,051 copies.\n- Timothy Leary was born on October 22, 1920, and was an American psychologist and writer known for advocating controlled exploration of the therapeutic potential of psychedelic drugs.\n- H. P. Lovecraft died on March 15, 1937.\n- Timothy Leary died on May 31, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
